@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Review of `harden-json-patch-values` found two gaps in `isJsonValue`: sparse array holes (`[ , 1]`, `new Array(3)`) pass because `Array.prototype.every` skips holes, and circular or very deeply nested values throw a raw `RangeError` (stack overflow) instead of `JsonPatchError`.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- A `value` containing a sparse array hole at any depth is rejected with `JsonPatchError` (a hole reads as `undefined`, which is not a JSON value).
+- A `value` that contains itself, or is nested deeper than a fixed limit, is rejected with `JsonPatchError` rather than overflowing the stack.
+- Not breaking for valid input: only values that were already outside the standard, or that crashed, change behaviour.
+
+**Governing standards:** RFC 8259 §3 (JSON values; JSON text is finite and has no holes or cycles), RFC 6902 §3, §4.1, §4.3, §4.6.
+
+**Out of scope:** validating the `document` argument, other operations, other error types.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+<!-- None -->
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: the "Patch document structure" requirement gains rules on holes, cycles and depth.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: `isJsonValue`.
+- `test/patch.test.ts`: new tests.
+- No new dependencies; no `package.json` change.
